<title>GERMANY: German airports release Sept cargo data.</title>
<headline>German airports release Sept cargo data.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table shows total, flown and trucked air cargo volumes in tonnes at international German airports in September 1996, according to the German airports association ADV.</p>
<p>    AIRPORT	     FLOWN  TRUCKED  TOTAL    % CHANGE</p>
<p>    Berlin (total)     2,703    511    3,214   +10.1</p>
<p>    - Tegel		1,493    488    1,98 1   +5.3</p>
<p>    - Tempelhof	     27	0	 27   +17.4</p>
<p>    - Schoenefeld	1,183     23    1,206   +18.9</p>
<p>    Bremen		   239  2,690    2,929   +29.5</p>
<p>    Dresden		  137    265	402    -3.1</p>
<p>    Duessseldorf	 5,213    n/a	n/a</p>
<p>    Frankfurt	  116,896    n/a	n/a</p>
<p>    Hamburg		3,008  2,724    5,732    +5.3</p>
<p>    Hannover		 970    n/a	n/a</p>
<p>    Cologne	     26,769  2,919   29,688   +14.7</p>
<p>    Leipzig/Halle	  261    115	376    -5.5</p>
<p>    Munich		 7,082    n/a	n/a</p>
<p>    Muenster/Osnabrueck   62  1,116    1,178    +4.5</p>
<p>    Nuremberg	    3,621  2,709    6,330    -4.0</p>
<p>    Saarbruecken	    32    168	200   +22.7</p>
<p>    Stuttgart	    1,708  4,548    6,256   +19.2</p>
<p>    TOTAL		168,701    n/a	n/a</p>
<p>Notes: No overall air cargo total is given as several large airports with known large trucking volumes including Frankfurt, Munich and Duesseldorf do not release trucking figures. --Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax +44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
